> Module Interest

> Using Types
> Using Params_2024 as P
> Using Rounding as R

# Interest income (Form 1040 lines 2a and 2b, Schedule B Part I)

Direct File module `interest.xml` (`../direct-file/direct-file/backend/src/main/resources/tax/interest.xml`,
"DF" below), scope.md section 3.3, issue #13. Tests:
`catala/tests/test_interest.catala_en` (named cases) and
`catala/tests/oracle_interest.catala_en` (generated, one scope per Direct File
scenario, compared with `oracle/facts.csv`).

Inputs are complete (`catala/CONVENTIONS.md` section 3): every box of every
interest report has a value, an empty box is `$0`. The top-level return scope
(#14) passes `has_foreign_accounts_or_trusts`, `filing_status`, `agi` and
`flow_has_seen_deductions` in; this module takes them as inputs until then.

## Statute and form

Interest is gross income (26 U.S.C. § 61(a)(4); § 61 is not among the files
in `sources/statute/`, so the form is the cited source). Form 1040 for 2024, `sources/forms-instructions/f1040--2024.pdf` p 1:
line 2a "Tax-exempt interest" and line 2b "Taxable interest".

Schedule B (Form 1040) 2024, `sources/forms-instructions/f1040sb--2024.pdf`
p 1, Part I line 4: "Subtract line 3 from line 2. Enter the result here and
on Form 1040 or 1040-SR, line 2b". Note under line 4: "If line 4 is over
$1,500, you must complete Part III." Part III: "You must complete this part if
you (a) had over $1,500 of taxable interest or ordinary dividends; (b) had a
foreign account; or (c) received a distribution from, or were a grantor of, or
a transferor to, a foreign trust."

Instructions for Schedule B, `sources/forms-instructions/i1040sb--2024.pdf`
p 1, General Instructions: "Use Schedule B (Form 1040) if any of the following
applies. You had over $1,500 of taxable interest or ordinary dividends. ... You
had a financial interest in, or signature authority over, a financial account
in a foreign country or you received a distribution from, or were a grantor
of, or transferor to, a foreign trust." Line 1: "Don't report on line 1 any
tax-exempt interest."

Rounding: the Form 1040 instructions (`i1040gi--2024.pdf` p 23) say "If you
have to add two or more amounts to figure the amount to enter on a line,
include cents when adding the amounts and round off only the total." Schedule B
line 1 lists one amount per payer, and line 4 is the sum of those listed
amounts; DF rounds each listed amount first, see `interest_income` below.

## One interest report (a Form 1099-INT, or interest without one)

DF collection `/interestReports` with children `/interestReports/*/x`. The DF
`Writable` children are fields of `InterestReport`; the `Derived` children are
outputs of the scope `InterestReportFacts`. The DF child `1099Amount` starts
with a digit, so it is `form_1099_amount` here.

```catala-metadata
## One entry of DF `/interestReports`: the boxes of a Form 1099-INT, or the
## amount of interest reported without one (`has_1099` false).
declaration structure InterestReport:
  # DF: /interestReports/*/filer (CollectionItem of /filers)
  data filer content Types.FilerRole
  # DF: /interestReports/*/has1099
  data has_1099 content boolean
  # DF: /interestReports/*/no1099Amount (Writable, used when has_1099 is false)
  data no_1099_amount content money
  # DF: /interestReports/*/writable1099Amount, 1099-INT box 1
  data writable_1099_amount content money
  # DF: /interestReports/*/writableEarlyWithdrawlPenaltyAmount, box 2
  data writable_early_withdrawl_penalty_amount content money
  # DF: /interestReports/*/writableInterestOnGovernmentBonds, box 3
  data writable_interest_on_government_bonds content money
  # DF: /interestReports/*/writableTaxWithheld, box 4
  data writable_tax_withheld content money
  # DF: /interestReports/*/writableForeignTaxPaid, box 6
  data writable_foreign_tax_paid content money
  # DF: /interestReports/*/writableTaxExemptInterest, box 8
  data writable_tax_exempt_interest content money
  # DF: /interestReports/*/writableSpecifiedPrivateActivityBondInterest, box 9
  data writable_specified_private_activity_bond_interest content money
  # DF: /interestReports/*/writableMarketDiscount, box 10
  data writable_market_discount content money
  # DF: /interestReports/*/writableBondPremium, box 11
  data writable_bond_premium content money
  # DF: /interestReports/*/writableBondPremiumOnTreasuryObligations, box 12
  data writable_bond_premium_on_treasury_obligations content money
  # DF: /interestReports/*/writableBondPremiumOnTaxExemptBond, box 13
  data writable_bond_premium_on_tax_exempt_bond content money
  # DF: /interestReports/*/writableState, box 15: true when the filer chose
  # `differentState` from /incomeFormStateOptions (`sameState` or no answer:
  # false).
  data state_is_different_state content boolean
  # DF: /interestReports/*/writableStateTaxWithheld, box 17
  data writable_state_tax_withheld content money
  # DF: /interestReports/*/factaFilingRequired (1099-INT FATCA box checked)
  data facta_filing_required content boolean
```

### Taxable interest of one report

Box 1 plus box 3 when there is a Form 1099-INT, else the amount entered
without one.

```catala-metadata
declaration scope InterestReportFacts:
  input report content InterestReport
  # DF: /interestReports/*/1099Amount
  output form_1099_amount content money
  # DF: /interestReports/*/interestOnGovernmentBonds
  output interest_on_government_bonds content money
  # DF: /interestReports/*/taxableInterest
  output taxable_interest content money
  # DF: /interestReports/*/roundedTaxableInterest
  output rounded_taxable_interest content money
  # DF: /interestReports/*/taxExemptInterest
  output tax_exempt_interest content money
  # DF: /interestReports/*/taxWithheld
  output tax_withheld content money
  # DF: /interestReports/*/foreignTaxPaid
  output foreign_tax_paid content money
  # DF: /interestReports/*/earlyWithdrawlPenaltyAmount
  output early_withdrawl_penalty_amount content money
  # Sum of boxes 9 to 13, the addend of DF /flowKnockoutHasBonds
  output bond_boxes_9_to_13 content money
  # DF: /interestReports/*/stateTaxWithheld
  output state_tax_withheld content money
  # DF: /interestReports/*/hasStateTaxWithheld
  output has_state_tax_withheld condition
  # DF: /interestReports/*/hasKnockoutWithholdingInDifferentState
  output has_knockout_withholding_in_different_state condition
  # Per-item part of DF /interestReports/hasRequiredFactaFilings
  output has_required_facta_filing condition
```

```catala
scope InterestReportFacts:
  # DF: /interestReports/*/1099Amount (the DF default $0 for an unanswered
  # box is the explicit $0 of a complete input).
  definition form_1099_amount equals report.writable_1099_amount

  # DF: /interestReports/*/interestOnGovernmentBonds: box 3 counts only when
  # there is a Form 1099-INT.
  definition interest_on_government_bonds equals
    if report.has_1099 then report.writable_interest_on_government_bonds
    else $0

  # Schedule B line 1 amount for this payer.
  # DF: /interestReports/*/taxableInterest
  definition taxable_interest equals
    if report.has_1099 then interest_on_government_bonds + form_1099_amount
    else report.no_1099_amount

  # Schedule B line 1 amount, to the whole dollar.
  # DF: /interestReports/*/roundedTaxableInterest
  definition rounded_taxable_interest equals R.round_dollar of taxable_interest

  # Box 8; $0 without a Form 1099-INT.
  # DF: /interestReports/*/taxExemptInterest
  definition tax_exempt_interest equals
    if report.has_1099 then report.writable_tax_exempt_interest else $0

  # Box 4, rounded to the whole dollar; $0 without a Form 1099-INT. Feeds
  # Form 1040 line 25b (taxCalculations.xml, fact at line 1428).
  # DF: /interestReports/*/taxWithheld
  definition tax_withheld equals
    R.round_dollar of
      (if report.has_1099 then report.writable_tax_withheld else $0)

  # Box 6; $0 without a Form 1099-INT.
  # DF: /interestReports/*/foreignTaxPaid
  definition foreign_tax_paid equals
    if report.has_1099 then report.writable_foreign_tax_paid else $0

  # Box 2. DF does not gate it on has1099.
  # DF: /interestReports/*/earlyWithdrawlPenaltyAmount
  definition early_withdrawl_penalty_amount equals
    report.writable_early_withdrawl_penalty_amount

  definition bond_boxes_9_to_13 equals
    report.writable_specified_private_activity_bond_interest
    + report.writable_market_discount
    + report.writable_bond_premium
    + report.writable_bond_premium_on_treasury_obligations
    + report.writable_bond_premium_on_tax_exempt_bond

  # DF: /interestReports/*/stateTaxWithheld
  definition state_tax_withheld equals report.writable_state_tax_withheld

  # DF: /interestReports/*/hasStateTaxWithheld
  rule has_state_tax_withheld under condition state_tax_withheld > $0
    consequence fulfilled

  # DF: /interestReports/*/hasKnockoutWithholdingInDifferentState
  rule has_knockout_withholding_in_different_state
    under condition report.state_is_different_state
    consequence fulfilled

  # The FATCA box counts only on a Form 1099-INT.
  # DF: /interestReports/hasRequiredFactaFilings (per-report condition)
  rule has_required_facta_filing
    under condition report.facta_filing_required and report.has_1099
    consequence fulfilled
```

## Form 1040 lines 2a and 2b, Schedule B requirement

```catala-metadata
declaration scope Interest:
  # DF: /interestReports (Writable collection)
  input interest_reports content list of InterestReport
  # DF: income.xml /hasForeignAccountsOrTrusts: the filer had a financial
  # interest in or signature authority over a foreign account, or was a
  # grantor of or had transactions with a foreign trust.
  # TODO(#14): derive from the three income.xml answers in the return scope.
  input has_foreign_accounts_or_trusts content boolean
  # Inputs of the NIIT-style knockouts only.
  input filing_status content Types.FilingStatus
  # DF: taxCalculations.xml /agi (Form 1040 line 11)
  input agi content money
  # DF: flow.xml /flowHasSeenDeductions. A UI hack: true once the filer has
  # seen the last deduction screen. The return scope (#14) passes true.
  input flow_has_seen_deductions content boolean

  internal facts content list of InterestReportFacts

  # DF: /requiresScheduleB (Form 1040 Schedule B filed)
  output requires_schedule_b condition
  # DF: /interestIncome (Form 1040 line 2b)
  output interest_income content money
  # DF: /taxExemptInterest (Form 1040 line 2a)
  output tax_exempt_interest content money
  # Form 1040 line 25b part from 1099-INT; DF sums
  # /interestReports/*/taxWithheld in taxCalculations.xml.
  output total_tax_withheld content money
  # DF: /hasInterestIncome
  output has_interest_income condition

  # Knockouts (catala/CONVENTIONS.md section 6; scope.md section 9 item 3).
  # DF: /flowKnockoutHasEarlyWithdrawlPenalty
  output ko_flow_knockout_has_early_withdrawl_penalty condition
  # DF: /flowKnockoutHasBonds
  output ko_flow_knockout_has_bonds condition
  # DF: /flowKnockoutHasForeignTaxPaid
  output ko_flow_knockout_has_foreign_tax_paid condition
  # DF: /flowKnockoutTaxExemptInterest
  output ko_flow_knockout_tax_exempt_interest condition
  # DF: /flowKnockoutStateTaxWithheld
  output ko_flow_knockout_state_tax_withheld condition
  # DF: /flowKnockoutWithholdingUnsupportedState
  output ko_flow_knockout_withholding_unsupported_state condition
  # DF: /interestReports/hasRequiredFactaFilings
  output ko_has_required_facta_filings condition
  # DF: /hasInterestIncomeAndAgiAboveThresholdForMfs
  output ko_has_interest_income_and_agi_above_threshold_for_mfs condition
  # DF: /hasInterestIncomeAndAgiAboveThresholdForMfjOrQss
  output ko_has_interest_income_and_agi_above_threshold_for_mfj_or_qss condition
  # DF: /hasInterestIncomeAndAgiAboveThresholdForSingleOrHoh
  output ko_has_interest_income_and_agi_above_threshold_for_single_or_hoh condition
  # All knockouts of this scope, listed once (flow.xml /flowIsKnockedOut
  # lines 21-26 and 61-64).
  output unsupported condition
```

### Line 2b: taxable interest

Schedule B line 1 lists the interest of each payer and line 4 adds them, "over
$1,500" requires Part III. The DF reference engine rounds each report to the
dollar and adds the rounded amounts when Schedule B is required, and rounds
the exact sum when it is not.

```catala
scope Interest:
  definition facts equals
    map each r among interest_reports to
      (output of InterestReportFacts with { -- report: r })

  # Schedule B, Part III: "You must complete this part if you (a) had over
  # $1,500 of taxable interest or ordinary dividends; (b) had a foreign
  # account; or (c) received a distribution from, or were a grantor of, or a
  # transferor to, a foreign trust." Only the interest half of (a) is in
  # scope: ordinary dividends are out of scope (scope.md section 1).
  # The comparison uses the unrounded sum of taxable interest.
  # DF: /requiresScheduleB (interest.xml)
  rule requires_schedule_b
    under condition
      (Money.sum of (map each f among facts to f.taxable_interest))
        > P.schedule_b_interest_threshold
      or has_foreign_accounts_or_trusts
    consequence fulfilled

  # QUIRK(Q-R1): DF sums per-item rounded amounts only when Schedule B is
  # required, and rounds the raw sum otherwise. The 1040 instructions (p 23)
  # say to add with cents and round only the total. Decision: reproduce
  # (CONVENTIONS.md section 8).
  # DF: interest.xml /interestIncome
  definition interest_income equals
    R.round_dollar of
      (if requires_schedule_b then
        Money.sum of (map each f among facts to f.rounded_taxable_interest)
       else
        Money.sum of (map each f among facts to f.taxable_interest))

  # DF: interest.xml /hasInterestIncome
  rule has_interest_income under condition interest_income > $0
    consequence fulfilled
```

### Line 2a: tax-exempt interest

Form 1040 line 2a is the sum of box 8 of every Form 1099-INT, rounded once to
the whole dollar. DF notes that it is "never used again outside of calculating
EITC eligibility and SSB taxibility".

```catala
scope Interest:
  # DF: interest.xml /taxExemptInterest
  definition tax_exempt_interest equals
    R.round_dollar of
      (Money.sum of (map each f among facts to f.tax_exempt_interest))

  # DF: taxCalculations.xml, sum of /interestReports/*/taxWithheld
  definition total_tax_withheld equals
    Money.sum of (map each f among facts to f.tax_withheld)
```

## Knockouts: 1099-INT boxes DF does not support

scope.md section 9 item 3: "1099-INT: early-withdrawal penalty, bonds, foreign
tax, tax-exempt interest, state withholding, FATCA". Each is a reason the
filer must use other software; the amounts are still computed.

```catala
scope Interest:
  # Box 2 over all reports is more than $0.
  # DF: /flowKnockoutHasEarlyWithdrawlPenalty
  rule ko_flow_knockout_has_early_withdrawl_penalty
    under condition
      (Money.sum of
        (map each f among facts to f.early_withdrawl_penalty_amount)) > $0
    consequence fulfilled

  # Boxes 9 to 13 summed over all reports is more than $0.
  # DF: /flowKnockoutHasBonds
  rule ko_flow_knockout_has_bonds
    under condition
      (Money.sum of (map each f among facts to f.bond_boxes_9_to_13)) > $0
    consequence fulfilled

  # Some report has a box 6 amount different from $0 (DF: NotEqual, so a
  # negative amount also counts).
  # DF: /flowKnockoutHasForeignTaxPaid
  rule ko_flow_knockout_has_foreign_tax_paid
    under condition exists f among facts such that f.foreign_tax_paid != $0
    consequence fulfilled

  # Some report has a box 8 amount different from $0.
  # DF: /flowKnockoutTaxExemptInterest
  rule ko_flow_knockout_tax_exempt_interest
    under condition exists f among facts such that f.tax_exempt_interest != $0
    consequence fulfilled

  # Some report has box 17 more than $0.
  # DF: /flowKnockoutStateTaxWithheld
  rule ko_flow_knockout_state_tax_withheld
    under condition exists f among facts such that f.has_state_tax_withheld
    consequence fulfilled

  # Some report has box 15 state `differentState`.
  # DF: /flowKnockoutWithholdingUnsupportedState
  rule ko_flow_knockout_withholding_unsupported_state
    under condition
      exists f among facts such that f.has_knockout_withholding_in_different_state
    consequence fulfilled

  # Some Form 1099-INT has the FATCA filing requirement box checked.
  # DF: /interestReports/hasRequiredFactaFilings
  rule ko_has_required_facta_filings
    under condition exists f among facts such that f.has_required_facta_filing
    consequence fulfilled
```

### Net investment income tax thresholds

26 U.S.C. § 1411(b) (`sources/statute/irc-1411.html`): "For purposes of this
chapter, the term "threshold amount" means (1) in the case of a taxpayer
making a joint return under section 6013 or a surviving spouse (as defined in
section 2(a)), $250,000, (2) in the case of a married taxpayer (as defined in
section 7703) filing a separate return, 1/2 of the dollar amount determined
under paragraph (1), and (3) in any other case, $200,000." DF does not
compute the tax: with interest income and an AGI above the threshold the
filer is knocked out, but only after the filer has seen the deduction screens
(final AGI). The `Params_2024` thresholds are the statute figures (`$250,000`,
`$125,000`, `$200,000`).

```catala
scope Interest:
  # DF: /hasInterestIncomeAndAgiAboveThresholdForMfs
  rule ko_has_interest_income_and_agi_above_threshold_for_mfs
    under condition
      flow_has_seen_deductions
      and filing_status = Types.FilingStatus.MarriedFilingSeparately
      and interest_income > $0
      and agi > P.niit_threshold_married_separate
    consequence fulfilled

  # DF: /hasInterestIncomeAndAgiAboveThresholdForMfjOrQss
  rule ko_has_interest_income_and_agi_above_threshold_for_mfj_or_qss
    under condition
      flow_has_seen_deductions
      and (filing_status = Types.FilingStatus.MarriedFilingJointly
           or filing_status = Types.FilingStatus.QualifyingSurvivingSpouse)
      and interest_income > $0
      and agi > P.niit_threshold_joint_or_surviving_spouse
    consequence fulfilled

  # DF: /hasInterestIncomeAndAgiAboveThresholdForSingleOrHoh
  rule ko_has_interest_income_and_agi_above_threshold_for_single_or_hoh
    under condition
      flow_has_seen_deductions
      and (filing_status = Types.FilingStatus.Single
           or filing_status = Types.FilingStatus.HeadOfHousehold)
      and interest_income > $0
      and agi > P.niit_threshold_other
    consequence fulfilled

  # DF: flow.xml /flowIsKnockedOut, the interest.xml members
  rule unsupported under condition
    ko_has_required_facta_filings
    or ko_flow_knockout_has_early_withdrawl_penalty
    or ko_flow_knockout_has_bonds
    or ko_flow_knockout_has_foreign_tax_paid
    or ko_flow_knockout_withholding_unsupported_state
    or ko_flow_knockout_state_tax_withheld
    or ko_has_interest_income_and_agi_above_threshold_for_mfs
    or ko_has_interest_income_and_agi_above_threshold_for_mfj_or_qss
    or ko_has_interest_income_and_agi_above_threshold_for_single_or_hoh
    or ko_flow_knockout_tax_exempt_interest
  consequence fulfilled
```
